  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DANIDA SPA 2022 Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) People can claim respect for, protection of, and fulfilment of, their rights 
The protective environment of Burundian and Congolese refugee communities, and Burundian returnees has improved with better capacity to access, claim and fulfil their rights.
Community-based protection groups are supported, and existing networks are strengthened
- Protection risks and trends faced by refugees, IDPs, and returnees are identified through protection monitoring and advocacy tailored to programming is conducted
- Case Management &amp; one-off cash assistance are conducted

2) People have more decent and resilient livelihoods 
Burundian and Congolese refugees, IDPs and host communities have increased resilience as a result of greater access to livelihoods and live more independently. 
- Community members have the livelihood skills and benefited vocational training
- Right holders have benefited the advantages of permagarden
- Right holders (Men and women) are economically empowered by cash for work assistance.
- Right holders have received IGA and Start-up Kits</narrative>
  </description>
